From 1efd83cf7e49e0d891761d9ca0efa208b73aade4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aamir <aamir@tallow-lang.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:59:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/27] extract: make the schema-first tier engine-agnostic,
 and off until configured
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two defects, one cause. The tier defaulted to ON while pointing at a local
service, so a run reported "attempted, failed" when the truth was "not
attempted" — and the engine actually chosen for it (the fleet's current model)
could not be pointed at at all, because the client spoke Ollama's API only.

Engine selection: `Engine::{Ollama, OpenAiCompatible}`, with Ollama kept and
dormant. `resolve_engine_config` refuses when no base URL is set — that refusal
IS the honest default, rather than a default that names a service the operator
has decided not to run. The model defaults to `deepseek/deepseek-flash` for the
cloud engine; an explicit TALLOW_LLM_MODEL/TALLOW_LLM_ENGINE overrides, and an
unknown engine name is refused instead of defaulted.

Availability is now backend-aware: the OpenAI-compatible path probes
`{base}/v1/models`, the cheapest question that separates reachable from not —
a bounded GET that cannot itself burn a completion or half an extraction.

The tier's state is measured, not inferred: `tier_state()` reports
{enabled, engine, engine_url, model, credential_present, reachable, reason}, and
`try_llm_fallback` records it as `llm_tier` in run evidence BEFORE deciding. A
tier that is not enabled returns without sending anything and records the reason
through the P4 limitation mechanism, so "no call was made" is visible instead of
looking like a failure.

Credential: TALLOW_LLM_API_KEY, read at call time, never stored on the
extractor, never argv, never a .tl literal; absent ⇒ refused
(EngineMisconfigured) rather than sent unauthenticated. Error text quotes URL
and status only, never a body that could echo the request.

Egress unchanged (P1.T3): the constructor still runs the zone predicate and
refuses rather than egressing direct, and the cloud call rides that same
client — no TALLOW_ALLOW_DIRECT-style bypass exists. The data-flow is stated in
the call's own doc comment: the vendor receives the page sample and the prompt;
with the guard intact the box IP does not leave the box.

Verified: cargo check --lib --bins RC=0; engine_tests 10 passed/0; the
smart_extract and llm_extract suites pass.
UNVERIFIED: the live call — it needs a credential and a reachable engine, so the
wire path remains plausible, not demonstrated.
Remaining from P1: T2's vault-backed custody, T5's compliance gate, T6's budget.
